WEBVTT

00:09.050 --> 00:11.052
[heavy rock music playing]

00:12.470 --> 00:15.223
♪ You make us sweat
By the trick for real ♪

00:18.601 --> 00:22.272
♪ You got a mind
And a tongue of silver so ♪

00:25.108 --> 00:28.278
♪ Please, oh, please, I gotta get out ♪

00:31.364 --> 00:35.368
♪ Ain't even kiddin'
We're the best, you diss yourself ♪

00:38.288 --> 00:41.207
♪ I can feel the same thing ♪

00:41.291 --> 00:44.502
♪ It's got me all like
A fever over me ♪

00:44.586 --> 00:49.132
♪ I ain't feelin' like that with myself ♪

00:49.215 --> 00:51.468
♪ So tell me how to find out ♪

00:53.053 --> 00:54.763
♪ Tell me how ♪

00:56.347 --> 00:58.600
If you're alive, make some noise!

00:58.683 --> 00:59.768
[cheering]

01:00.560 --> 01:01.686
You're alive!

01:01.770 --> 01:03.104
[cheering]

01:03.772 --> 01:06.483
♪ I can feel the same thing ♪

01:07.067 --> 01:09.819
♪ It's got me all like
A fever over me ♪

01:09.903 --> 01:14.699
♪ I ain't feelin' like that with myself ♪

01:14.783 --> 01:16.951
♪ So tell me how to find out ♪

01:21.790 --> 01:23.208
♪ Tell me how ♪

01:24.793 --> 01:26.753
♪ Tell me how ♪

01:28.254 --> 01:30.632
- ♪ Tell me how ♪
- [loud cheering and whistling]

01:39.307 --> 01:41.518
[whistling and cheering continues]

01:49.025 --> 01:50.735
[cheering fades]

01:51.820 --> 01:53.238
[Kyuma yawns] Uh…

01:54.364 --> 01:55.323
[grunts]

01:55.949 --> 01:57.867
What was our, uh, score today?

01:58.701 --> 02:00.036
[Shitara] Five hundred points.

02:00.120 --> 02:01.621
- [Uta] Five hundred? That's high.
- Whoa.

02:01.704 --> 02:03.581
[Goken] Maki only earned three.

02:03.665 --> 02:06.960
- [Shitara] I'm worth at least five.
- [laughs] That's hilarious.

02:07.043 --> 02:07.961
[Shitara] Brutal.

02:09.045 --> 02:11.422
Hell of a show though, huh? We crushed it.

02:11.506 --> 02:13.842
- [Uta] The crowd was really into it.
- [Shitara] Yeah.

02:15.385 --> 02:17.137
[Kyuma] Okay, listen up.

02:17.220 --> 02:19.806
- [Shitara] Listening.
- We need today's driver, yeah?

02:20.390 --> 02:22.684
- We'll point at them on three.
- [Shitara] Yeah?

02:22.767 --> 02:23.810
- You point.
- [Uta] Point?

02:23.893 --> 02:25.395
- Yeah, on three. Shit.
- [Uta] Okay.

02:25.478 --> 02:27.230
- Whoever did the worst today.
- [Kyuma] Yeah.

02:27.313 --> 02:28.773
- Right?
- [Uta laughs] Okay.

02:28.857 --> 02:31.109
- [Kyuma] On three.
- [Goken] I know who I'm picking.

02:31.192 --> 02:32.610
- You ready?
- [Shitara] Sure.

02:33.528 --> 02:35.405
- Let's…
- [Maki and Goken] Okay!

02:35.488 --> 02:37.198
[all] One, two--

02:50.295 --> 02:52.463
We're the citizens of this country.

02:55.425 --> 02:56.426
Citizens?

02:56.509 --> 02:58.094
Sure. Citizens.

02:58.720 --> 03:00.096
[Kuina] What do you mean?

03:00.180 --> 03:01.681
We're all living here, right?

03:02.265 --> 03:03.349
Who can say?

03:05.935 --> 03:07.645
In this place, I'm the leader.

03:08.855 --> 03:10.732
We created this game.

03:10.815 --> 03:14.235
That man, Shitara? All his idea.

03:14.819 --> 03:18.031
Well, to be fair,
this is a brand-new experience for us.

03:18.114 --> 03:20.575
We haven't played a game of it yet
as a team.

03:22.577 --> 03:25.872
What does that mean?
We're competing against citizens now?

03:25.955 --> 03:27.498
Us against the five of you?

03:27.582 --> 03:28.541
[Kyuma] Yeah.

03:29.042 --> 03:31.169
When you play a face card game,

03:31.252 --> 03:34.172
you're competing against citizens
fighting for their lives.

03:34.672 --> 03:36.549
Anyone who loses is killed.

03:37.133 --> 03:38.051
So…

03:39.427 --> 03:43.097
these are games of life or death
for us citizens as well.

03:46.517 --> 03:47.977
It's time to begin.

03:49.520 --> 03:51.731
The game we'll be playing is…

03:53.650 --> 03:56.027
[computer over PA]
Difficulty, King of Clubs.

03:56.736 --> 03:57.737
Game…

03:58.905 --> 04:00.073
Osmosis.

04:00.156 --> 04:01.991
[tense, grinding music]

04:02.075 --> 04:04.077
Osmosis…

04:18.091 --> 04:20.093
[theme music]

05:21.612 --> 05:23.281
Now, the rules are simple.

05:24.240 --> 05:25.241
[chiming]

05:25.325 --> 05:27.535
The game lasts two hours.

05:27.618 --> 05:29.787
Both teams try to collect points.

05:29.871 --> 05:33.082
The team with the highest total
at the end of the game wins.

05:34.584 --> 05:37.420
Each team begins with 10,000 points.

05:37.503 --> 05:41.341
Players divide these points
amongst themselves before the game begins.

05:42.925 --> 05:45.386
The minimum amount is 100 points.

05:45.470 --> 05:48.014
You're free to divide them up
any way you want.

05:48.097 --> 05:50.224
Talk it over as a team and decide.

05:51.351 --> 05:55.355
Points distribution is a key element
of strategy in this game.

05:57.690 --> 05:59.359
[electronic music]

06:00.234 --> 06:01.903
How does one earn points?

06:02.779 --> 06:05.782
There are three ways
you can do so in this game.

06:06.532 --> 06:10.745
Battle, items, and base.

06:10.828 --> 06:12.121
[Kuina sighs] Hold on!

06:12.622 --> 06:13.873
Yeah, you got a question?

06:14.540 --> 06:16.459
How do we remember all this?

06:16.542 --> 06:18.252
- [laughs]
- [Kyuma] Right.

06:18.336 --> 06:21.297
- I guess it's easier once you do it, huh?
- [whirring]

06:21.381 --> 06:24.550
A demonstration.
You've got random points for now.

06:25.635 --> 06:28.721
Your bracelet shows
your individual points.

06:28.805 --> 06:30.014
[clunk]

06:30.723 --> 06:32.016
Let's try a battle.

06:32.892 --> 06:34.185
ARISU

06:34.268 --> 06:38.106
A battle's outcome depends entirely
on your current points.

06:38.689 --> 06:42.443
To initiate one,
all you need to do is touch your opponent.

06:42.527 --> 06:43.653
Hey!

06:45.863 --> 06:47.198
[bracelet chimes]

06:47.281 --> 06:50.493
NIRAGI 2,000
KYUMA 3,500

06:50.576 --> 06:52.787
[Kyuma] Whoever has more points wins.

06:52.870 --> 06:55.790
The winner steals 500 points
from the loser.

06:55.873 --> 06:57.834
[chiming]

07:01.045 --> 07:02.255
[PA chimes]

07:02.338 --> 07:05.675
The scores have been updated.

07:07.510 --> 07:09.178
[chiming]

07:10.138 --> 07:13.850
The King of Clubs team
is now leading by 1,000 points.

07:18.396 --> 07:19.564
[beep]

07:21.482 --> 07:22.358
[beep]

07:22.442 --> 07:23.317
ARISU

07:23.401 --> 07:26.320
[Arisu] So you don't know
your opponent's score until you battle.

07:26.404 --> 07:28.865
No. You know what that means, right?

07:28.948 --> 07:31.159
It means these battles are a huge gamble,

07:31.242 --> 07:33.786
where you're unable
to see your opponent's strength.

07:33.870 --> 07:37.290
Something else you can try
is to pair up with a teammate.

07:38.124 --> 07:39.375
For example…

07:40.543 --> 07:43.004
You two. Try holding hands.

07:47.842 --> 07:51.012
Oh wow, what's this?
[chuckles] A bit nervous, are ya?

08:03.357 --> 08:05.359
Would you look at that? Cute couple.

08:07.820 --> 08:10.948
All right.
If teammates hold hands like this,

08:11.032 --> 08:13.576
they're able to battle
using their combined points,

08:13.659 --> 08:16.829
allowing them to beat an opponent
they couldn't defeat on their own.

08:19.207 --> 08:20.625
[chiming]

08:21.209 --> 08:23.669
The winners get the 500
divided between them.

08:27.882 --> 08:28.883
Cuties.

08:30.009 --> 08:31.260
On to items!

08:31.844 --> 08:33.721
ITEM

08:34.305 --> 08:38.893
There are items for you to find, six
of them, hidden amongst the containers.

08:38.976 --> 08:40.978
[chiming]

08:41.062 --> 08:42.522
[Tatta] Ugh, this area's huge!

08:42.605 --> 08:45.775
[Kuina] There are only six items
in all these shipping containers?

08:45.858 --> 08:49.111
Touching an item
will earn your team some points.

08:49.820 --> 08:51.697
And finally, we come to these poles.

08:51.781 --> 08:53.950
Bases are a big part of the game.

08:54.033 --> 08:55.910
- [whirring]
- They can turn the tide.

08:55.993 --> 08:57.995
[buzzing]

08:59.956 --> 09:04.210
This pole is your base.
Ours is on the other side.

09:04.293 --> 09:05.336
BASE

09:06.754 --> 09:09.549
If you manage to touch
your opponents' base,

09:10.675 --> 09:12.260
10,000 points are yours.

09:12.343 --> 09:16.264
10,000 points?
Don't both teams start with that?

09:16.347 --> 09:20.184
Exactly why you need to keep someone back
to protect your base.

09:20.268 --> 09:25.147
But while a player is touching
their own base, they have infinite points.

09:26.023 --> 09:27.149
Infinite?

09:28.484 --> 09:31.028
How do you battle someone
with infinite points?

09:34.615 --> 09:35.741
[Kyuma] Come here.

09:39.912 --> 09:41.914
[electricity humming]

09:50.298 --> 09:51.507
[chimes]

09:52.008 --> 09:54.385
ARISU 2,250
KYUMA INFINITE

09:54.468 --> 09:58.139
[Kyuma] I was touching my base,
so you lose 10,000 points.

09:58.222 --> 09:59.515
ARISU -7,750
KYUMA 3,500

09:59.599 --> 10:01.225
And I gain 10,000.

10:03.603 --> 10:05.354
ARISU -7,750
KYUMA 13,500

10:05.938 --> 10:07.064
Hang on…

10:08.107 --> 10:09.817
So what would happen to him?

10:09.900 --> 10:11.986
His score would have dropped below zero.

10:12.820 --> 10:13.821
Pyeeow.

10:14.405 --> 10:15.364
Shot down.

10:18.993 --> 10:20.828
If you try to touch the other team's base

10:21.412 --> 10:25.833
and their goalie manages to touch you,
you lose 10,000 points.

10:27.001 --> 10:31.464
You die, and the opposing team
gains 10,000 points?

10:32.798 --> 10:34.008
That's way too risky.

10:34.091 --> 10:36.761
If you pull it off,
you can change everything.

10:40.389 --> 10:41.724
[Kyuma] Something else.

10:42.308 --> 10:45.478
After completing a battle
or touching the other team's base,

10:45.561 --> 10:47.229
players are temporarily out of commission.

10:47.313 --> 10:48.230
INACTIVE

10:48.314 --> 10:51.150
During this time, their points are frozen.
They're immune.

10:51.233 --> 10:54.028
If you touch an opponent
while they're out of commission…

10:54.111 --> 10:55.738
[electricity crackling]

10:55.821 --> 10:58.491
…your wristband will give you
an electric shock.

10:58.574 --> 11:01.661
Enough to knock you out, so be careful.

11:02.536 --> 11:04.080
Once you touch your own base,

11:04.163 --> 11:07.124
your status is reset
and you can resume play.

11:10.419 --> 11:15.299
So, you know the rules. Split up
your points now, then the game begins.

11:21.389 --> 11:22.306
[Arisu] Hold on.

11:26.894 --> 11:28.062
I'm Arisu.

11:30.022 --> 11:30.940
Kyuma…

11:32.733 --> 11:35.778
tell me something, before we fight.

11:38.656 --> 11:40.616
If we beat all the games here,

11:42.993 --> 11:44.704
will we go back to our world?

11:48.749 --> 11:51.460
[Kyuma] Your world? What is your world?

11:53.587 --> 11:55.631
The way that you're speaking about it,

11:57.258 --> 12:00.594
you're making it sound
like your world must be the real one.

12:02.638 --> 12:04.390
[Arisu] What are you talking about?

12:05.766 --> 12:06.934
Tell me something.

12:07.435 --> 12:10.521
How many real conversations did you have?

12:10.604 --> 12:12.815
How many heart-to-hearts did you have?

12:14.191 --> 12:16.360
Our flaws, our pride.

12:17.778 --> 12:20.114
Those are exposed here, in this world.

12:22.366 --> 12:24.034
When we look death in the eye,

12:24.869 --> 12:27.663
we face true human nature and reality.

12:32.877 --> 12:36.005
This world is more real
than any you left behind.

12:36.714 --> 12:38.841
These games are conversations.

12:40.050 --> 12:41.761
Let's really talk, you and I.

12:42.344 --> 12:44.388
Let us expose our true hearts.

12:44.472 --> 12:45.389
Arisu.

12:47.183 --> 12:48.976
You want the truth, yeah?

12:50.060 --> 12:52.229
Face me with everything you have.

12:54.732 --> 12:56.400
[tense music]

13:04.366 --> 13:05.659
All right, then.

13:07.912 --> 13:09.455
[sighs] I'll play your game.

13:19.381 --> 13:22.968
Is it just me,
or was Kyuma being nice to us?

13:23.052 --> 13:24.512
Just like a normal guy.

13:24.595 --> 13:27.640
Buck naked and crazy. Yeah, real normal.

13:27.723 --> 13:30.142
This game'll be a bloodbath,
just like all the others.

13:32.019 --> 13:33.103
Okay.

13:33.604 --> 13:35.564
Let's distribute the points.

13:36.065 --> 13:38.818
How many do we each get? Got any ideas?

13:38.901 --> 13:40.820
[wind whistling]

13:41.320 --> 13:42.321
Split 'em five ways, no?

13:42.404 --> 13:45.074
We're not going to win
splitting them evenly between us.

13:47.910 --> 13:49.078
[Arisu] Usagi's right.

13:49.745 --> 13:53.290
It's like Kyuma said.
It's an important decision for the game.

13:53.374 --> 13:55.084
The initial point split is crucial.

13:55.835 --> 13:57.336
You got a plan or what?

14:04.301 --> 14:05.636
[energetic, tense music]

14:05.719 --> 14:07.680
[computer, echoing] Game start.

14:25.573 --> 14:27.700
Whooooo!

14:41.005 --> 14:42.423
[Arisu] Here's the plan.

14:42.506 --> 14:44.884
The faster runners get fewer points.

14:45.551 --> 14:47.678
Slower runners get more.

14:49.930 --> 14:53.309
The guard at the base
gets the least number of points possible.

14:54.894 --> 14:58.731
We go out in pairs,
one fast runner with one slower runner.

14:59.732 --> 15:01.859
Why'd you pair up with me, anyway?

15:02.359 --> 15:03.944
You like me that much, huh?

15:04.028 --> 15:06.822
Please. Because I won't care
if you die in front of me.

15:06.906 --> 15:08.032
[laughs]

15:08.782 --> 15:11.076
[Arisu] Pairing up for battles
has many advantages,

15:11.160 --> 15:14.788
but one of the biggest
is they can only see your combined points.

15:14.872 --> 15:17.458
They won't know
how many points you each have.

15:23.213 --> 15:24.965
[panting]

15:31.805 --> 15:33.849
We've got 5,000 between us.

15:33.933 --> 15:35.517
He won't have more than that.

15:35.601 --> 15:37.895
They'd be crazy
to give one person half their points.

15:38.938 --> 15:41.523
- Let's get him.
- Yeah, let's get it done.

15:46.654 --> 15:47.988
[chiming]

15:49.406 --> 15:50.783
Uh-oh…

15:54.411 --> 15:55.371
Huh?

15:57.289 --> 15:59.333
Guess he didn't have that many after all.

16:11.428 --> 16:12.972
[Kuina] Nothing here either.

16:16.016 --> 16:17.601
No. Come on.

16:24.733 --> 16:28.529
Hey. Why'd you pair up Usagi with Niragi?

16:28.612 --> 16:29.530
Strategy.

16:30.072 --> 16:32.282
[sighs] What's going on with you two?

16:32.783 --> 16:34.034
What do you mean?

16:35.119 --> 16:36.203
Arisu…

16:37.788 --> 16:40.416
If something's changed
between you and Usagi,

16:40.499 --> 16:41.917
shouldn't you tell us?

16:42.918 --> 16:45.087
No, we're fine. It's fine, okay?

16:46.714 --> 16:47.965
If you say so.

16:52.678 --> 16:53.595
Oh!

16:53.679 --> 16:55.014
[Kuina] Is that an item?

17:13.699 --> 17:16.118
KUINA
ITEM

17:16.201 --> 17:17.411
[chimes]

17:21.415 --> 17:22.458
2,000 points!

17:23.333 --> 17:24.209
Awesome!

17:25.753 --> 17:26.920
- Yes!
- Yes!

17:27.004 --> 17:30.132
[computer] The player team
has secured an item.

17:30.215 --> 17:34.386
The player team is now leading
by 2,000 points.

17:34.470 --> 17:37.056
- We're winning!
- Yeah, that's pretty cool!

17:40.100 --> 17:41.268
Congratulations.

17:41.935 --> 17:43.103
[both gasp]

17:46.023 --> 17:48.442
Look, we can't avoid each other forever.

17:48.525 --> 17:49.735
You wanna battle or what?

17:52.404 --> 17:53.822
ARISU

17:53.906 --> 17:55.824
KUINA

18:04.291 --> 18:05.501
[chiming]

18:08.253 --> 18:09.797
[Kuina gasps]

18:09.880 --> 18:11.548
Stay close, Arisu.

18:12.049 --> 18:14.676
It's two on one. We'll take it slow.

18:15.344 --> 18:16.512
[Arisu] Yeah.

18:19.556 --> 18:21.600
I couldn't help but overhear.

18:22.101 --> 18:23.602
Sounds like there's an issue.

18:24.311 --> 18:26.271
You're fighting
with one of your teammates.

18:33.112 --> 18:34.071
Arisu,

18:35.989 --> 18:37.825
you have a certain strength about you.

18:39.076 --> 18:41.120
The look of someone who has faced death.

18:41.995 --> 18:43.747
A man will do whatever it takes.

18:44.832 --> 18:46.291
That's why it's so strange.

18:46.375 --> 18:49.628
Your confidence…
Why on earth would it be shaken now?

18:54.633 --> 18:56.718
The five of us were in a band before.

18:57.845 --> 18:59.721
Sometimes we would disagree,

19:00.389 --> 19:02.641
and yet they'd be behind me
at the end of the day.

19:03.142 --> 19:06.770
And so…
I learned something about being a leader.

19:07.855 --> 19:10.607
You can't push people
into following you for no reason.

19:11.608 --> 19:13.735
You have to be ready to listen.

19:13.819 --> 19:15.529
Wait for them to come to you.

19:17.156 --> 19:20.868
Do that,
and they'll know they can depend on you.

19:27.207 --> 19:28.208
Now,

19:29.418 --> 19:30.502
let's go.

19:37.009 --> 19:39.636
Don't hesitate! Not today!

19:40.137 --> 19:43.182
We could die. We all could.
Me, my friends, and you.

19:43.265 --> 19:44.183
Arisu.

19:45.184 --> 19:47.686
Let's not end our lives with regret.

19:47.769 --> 19:48.854
If you're gonna die,

19:49.730 --> 19:52.191
wouldn't you rather give it
everything you've got?

20:06.205 --> 20:07.247
Arisu?

20:09.625 --> 20:10.626
Kyuma.

20:11.877 --> 20:13.212
You said that

20:14.087 --> 20:18.258
to learn the truth, I have to face you
with everything I've got.

20:19.384 --> 20:20.260
Yeah.

20:22.512 --> 20:24.640
I wanna learn more about who you are.

20:25.807 --> 20:27.392
So battle me alone, Kyuma.

20:32.814 --> 20:34.775
[gasps] Arisu?

20:39.279 --> 20:40.489
You've got it.

20:50.290 --> 20:51.625
[chiming]

20:54.836 --> 20:56.922
ARISU 4,600
KYUMA 2,000

20:57.005 --> 20:58.840
- [PA chimes]
- Gah!

20:58.924 --> 21:01.551
- [computer] The scores have been updated.
- [Kyuma] I lost!

21:01.635 --> 21:03.428
[Arisu] 2,000 points?

21:03.512 --> 21:06.223
[computer] The player team is now leading
by 3,000 points.

21:06.306 --> 21:07.808
ARISU INACTIVE

21:10.811 --> 21:11.937
Wait a sec.

21:12.437 --> 21:14.273
Did you give everyone equal points?

21:14.898 --> 21:17.693
Yeah, everyone got 2,000.

21:18.527 --> 21:20.654
I thought this was
a game of life or death.

21:23.824 --> 21:25.075
Here's what I think.

21:25.158 --> 21:27.703
My four teammates and I are equals.

21:28.245 --> 21:29.871
We live or die together.

21:33.834 --> 21:37.546
So, Arisu,
did you learn something just now?

21:46.263 --> 21:47.889
[urgent music]

22:06.199 --> 22:07.117
Oh!

22:11.413 --> 22:12.497
[grunting]

22:14.666 --> 22:16.001
- Ha!
- [chime]

22:16.084 --> 22:17.753
Ah! You got me!

22:17.836 --> 22:18.754
- Gah!
- [laughs]

22:18.837 --> 22:22.341
- Yeah!
- [computer] The scores have been updated.

22:22.424 --> 22:27.179
The player team is now leading
by 4,000 points.

22:28.638 --> 22:29.598
Okay.

22:46.490 --> 22:47.616
[chime]

22:48.533 --> 22:51.119
[computer] The scores have been updated.

22:51.203 --> 22:53.372
- [both] Yes!
- [computer] The player team is leading…

22:53.455 --> 22:54.915
I'm sorry.

22:54.998 --> 22:56.041
[tuts]

22:59.169 --> 23:01.171
All right, you guys! [laughs]

23:01.880 --> 23:03.507
Things are going great so far.

23:03.590 --> 23:06.635
This is a King game? Don't make me laugh.

23:06.718 --> 23:07.886
- [Tatta] Yeah!
- Hah!

23:07.969 --> 23:09.346
Yeah! Yeah!

23:09.429 --> 23:10.889
Pretty crazy to think…

23:10.972 --> 23:13.767
But I almost forgot
you're one of the bad guys, Niragi.

23:13.850 --> 23:14.684
Huh.

23:23.068 --> 23:24.820
[whirring]

23:31.159 --> 23:32.661
ARISU

23:32.744 --> 23:34.329
[Tatta] Well, what'd you learn?

23:35.038 --> 23:37.833
- [Arisu] They split the points evenly.
- [Usagi] Evenly? Are you sure?

23:37.916 --> 23:40.377
- [coughs]
- [Kuina] 2,000 each, yup.

23:40.460 --> 23:43.797
[Arisu] We need to keep the pressure on.
And find more items if we can.

23:43.880 --> 23:45.382
- [Usagi] Right.
- [Tatta]Yeah.

23:45.465 --> 23:47.467
[Arisu] Tatta, you got this, buddy.

23:48.760 --> 23:49.803
[Tatta] Thanks.

23:56.601 --> 23:57.978
[sighs]

24:02.774 --> 24:05.610
They're up by 5,000. I can't believe it.

24:06.111 --> 24:07.904
This is absolute bullshit!

24:08.697 --> 24:10.949
So, what do we do, o leader? Huh?

24:11.575 --> 24:12.617
[chuckles]

24:12.701 --> 24:14.035
They're certainly not bad.

24:14.119 --> 24:15.704
Huh? Oh, this is funny to you?

24:16.371 --> 24:20.167
Splitting the points up evenly
was your plan, Kyuma. You figure it out!

24:20.250 --> 24:21.835
Hey, chill out, dude.

24:22.502 --> 24:25.338
This isn't some dictatorship.
He didn't decide for us.

24:26.798 --> 24:28.258
We did it together.

24:28.341 --> 24:31.761
Just like we've always done,
and just like we're going to keep doing.

24:32.471 --> 24:33.889
Absolutely!

24:33.972 --> 24:35.056
So what do we do?

24:35.807 --> 24:36.766
Yo, Maki!

24:38.101 --> 24:39.394
Yeah, man, we all heard you.

24:39.478 --> 24:40.937
So why don't you say something?

24:41.021 --> 24:42.939
[Maki sighs, tuts]

24:43.023 --> 24:44.774
- [Maki scoffs]
- [Kyuma] I do have one idea.

24:44.858 --> 24:47.819
Me too. I've got an idea,

24:47.903 --> 24:49.821
if you don't mind something crazy.

24:51.072 --> 24:52.115
[chuckles]

24:52.199 --> 24:54.951
[Kyuma] How funny would it be
if it was the same idea?

24:55.827 --> 24:58.163
Well, how about if we say it on three?

24:58.246 --> 24:59.289
Let's go.

25:01.041 --> 25:02.292
[both] One, two…

25:02.375 --> 25:04.794
[wind whistling]

25:04.878 --> 25:05.795
[chime]

25:06.505 --> 25:09.633
[computer]
The player team has secured an item.

25:10.383 --> 25:14.971
The player team is now leading
by 6,000 points.

25:15.889 --> 25:16.932
Yes!

25:30.862 --> 25:31.947
[gasps]

25:32.989 --> 25:34.115
[Kyuma] Hey.

26:03.436 --> 26:04.771
Why are you all here?

26:04.854 --> 26:07.065
We're here so we can win, man.

26:09.693 --> 26:11.111
[breathing shakily]

26:13.113 --> 26:14.114
[gasps]

26:20.745 --> 26:21.830
[crackling]

26:21.913 --> 26:23.164
[buzzing]

26:25.875 --> 26:27.627
TATTA
INFINITE

26:30.797 --> 26:31.673
You…

26:32.591 --> 26:33.592
I've got…

26:34.175 --> 26:35.468
I've got infinite points!

26:35.552 --> 26:37.387
[breathing shakily]

26:40.432 --> 26:41.933
You get tagged here…

26:43.935 --> 26:44.894
and you'll die!

26:50.066 --> 26:51.151
You're right.

26:51.985 --> 26:54.279
And since it's a game of life or death,

26:55.322 --> 26:57.532
why don't you tell us
who dies by your hand?

26:58.992 --> 27:02.203
What? But you'll be killed!

27:04.080 --> 27:04.998
You'll die!

27:06.666 --> 27:07.751
Stay back!

27:11.129 --> 27:12.005
No! Don't!

27:17.719 --> 27:18.928
Ah! Ah!

27:19.012 --> 27:19.971
[yells]

27:22.182 --> 27:24.809
[computer] The scores have been updated.

27:28.730 --> 27:33.234
The King of Club team
is now leading by 4,000 points.

27:33.318 --> 27:34.569
[Arisu] They overtook us.

27:35.987 --> 27:37.364
[sighs] What the hell?

27:38.990 --> 27:41.493
[computer] One player
on the King of Clubs team

27:41.576 --> 27:44.079
has had their score fall below zero.

27:47.832 --> 27:49.167
[gasps]

27:53.755 --> 27:54.964
You picked me?

27:56.508 --> 27:58.677
[panting]

28:06.434 --> 28:08.061
You better use this to win.

28:09.771 --> 28:11.606
If I die in vain, I'm…

28:12.482 --> 28:16.319
I'm gonna beat the shit out of you
in the afterlife, man. [sobs]

28:16.403 --> 28:19.155
[computer] It is game over for the player.

28:21.157 --> 28:22.951
[breathing shakily]

28:25.286 --> 28:26.329
Shitara.

28:27.622 --> 28:28.915
You were my good friend.

28:29.666 --> 28:31.626
I'll never forget what you did for us.

28:33.461 --> 28:34.629
[gasping]

28:37.340 --> 28:38.508
Later, man.

28:45.181 --> 28:46.725
[gasping]

29:08.496 --> 29:09.748
Shitara.

29:22.844 --> 29:24.471
[breathing shakily]

29:46.117 --> 29:47.160
Shitara.

30:08.264 --> 30:10.600
They sacrificed a member of their team.

30:12.185 --> 30:14.854
Now three of them have 10,000 points each.

30:15.772 --> 30:17.982
[Niragi]
Couldn't even guard one pole, huh?

30:18.066 --> 30:19.609
[laughing] Fucking useless.

30:19.692 --> 30:22.153
Trash is always gonna be trash.

30:22.237 --> 30:23.822
You piece of shit!

30:23.905 --> 30:27.450
- Lay off of him. He did the best he could.
- The best he could?

30:28.034 --> 30:31.037
You get a chance to kill one of them,
obviously you kill Kyuma!

30:31.120 --> 30:33.081
It's not that. We underestimated them.

30:33.581 --> 30:37.669
He was nice and we got sucked in,
so we forgot the most important thing.

30:38.253 --> 30:39.671
Kyuma is the King of Clubs.

30:39.754 --> 30:42.465
We forgot
that we're gambling with our lives.

30:42.549 --> 30:43.967
[Niragi scoffs]

30:44.050 --> 30:45.510
They're prepared to die.

30:46.094 --> 30:47.595
They've just shown us that.

30:48.680 --> 30:51.057
If we don't do something,
we're all finished.

30:57.981 --> 30:59.649
Only one hour left on the clock.

31:02.735 --> 31:05.071
We can turn this around
if we attack their base.

31:05.154 --> 31:07.365
We can't get to their base
if they're defending it.

31:07.448 --> 31:10.743
- Yeah, Niragi's right.
- Then how do we win this thing?

31:11.452 --> 31:16.165
Split up again.
Forget battling. Items are the key.

31:16.749 --> 31:19.085
That's the only way
we're getting out of this alive.

31:19.586 --> 31:21.296
- Come on. Hurry!
- [Niragi groans]

31:42.692 --> 31:43.776
[PA chimes]

31:44.569 --> 31:48.072
[computer] The King of Clubs team
has secured an item.

31:49.532 --> 31:53.620
The King of Clubs team is now leading
by 4,500 points.

31:53.703 --> 31:55.330
Well, that ain't good.

31:58.291 --> 31:59.334
[gasps]

32:04.547 --> 32:05.465
[chuckles]

32:13.264 --> 32:14.182
Got ya.

32:14.265 --> 32:15.475
- [gasps]
- [chiming]

32:16.726 --> 32:19.604
[computer] The scores have been updated.

32:20.897 --> 32:25.360
The King of Clubs team is now leading
by 5,500 points.

32:29.656 --> 32:32.992
The King of Clubs team
has secured an item.

32:34.369 --> 32:38.373
The King of Clubs team
is now leading by 7,000 points.

32:38.456 --> 32:40.166
We're so fucked.

32:50.593 --> 32:51.678
You alone? [laughs]

32:57.058 --> 32:59.102
Let's do this, you and me.

33:00.812 --> 33:02.271
You ought to know

33:02.355 --> 33:03.856
I'm making you work for this.

33:06.150 --> 33:07.652
[exhales]

33:10.196 --> 33:12.198
All I need is one punch.

33:13.116 --> 33:14.701
You win this battle,

33:14.784 --> 33:16.786
you'll be out cold for the rest.

33:20.665 --> 33:21.874
[yells]

33:26.671 --> 33:27.880
[squeals]

33:27.964 --> 33:29.549
- [gasping]
- [chiming]

33:31.968 --> 33:33.594
[groans]

33:35.096 --> 33:36.139
KUINA
INACTIVE

33:36.222 --> 33:37.640
[sighs]

33:37.724 --> 33:39.183
Why'd you let me brag, dude?

33:39.267 --> 33:40.977
I didn't know you could fight.

33:41.060 --> 33:42.228
- [Maki scoffs]
- [PA chimes]

33:42.311 --> 33:43.187
[groans]

33:43.271 --> 33:45.940
[computer] The scores have been updated.

33:46.024 --> 33:47.275
[Arisu] What are they doing?

33:47.358 --> 33:51.404
[computer] The King of Clubs team
is now leading by 8,000 points.

34:11.591 --> 34:12.467
[Uta] Sorry!

34:12.550 --> 34:14.302
- [Arisu yelps]
- Snooze, you lose.

34:19.640 --> 34:21.225
Yes! 3,000!

34:21.726 --> 34:23.728
- [Kyuma] The most valuable item.
- [gasps]

34:26.522 --> 34:27.940
[Arisu] What the hell?

34:28.024 --> 34:29.400
If you're both here, then…

34:30.818 --> 34:31.736
Wait.

34:32.528 --> 34:34.739
There's no one guarding your base?

34:34.822 --> 34:35.698
[Kyuma] Nope.

34:36.282 --> 34:39.035
We figured that you wouldn't have
the guts to invade ours.

34:39.118 --> 34:40.828
And we were right, weren't we?

34:43.081 --> 34:44.665
I can't believe this.

34:46.626 --> 34:47.877
[sobbing]

34:48.795 --> 34:51.255
[Kyuma] You told me
you wanted answers, Arisu.

34:54.258 --> 34:56.677
The games are cruel. You know that.

34:57.762 --> 35:00.515
The value of a single life
is meaningless here.

35:01.390 --> 35:02.225
Look at me.

35:03.267 --> 35:04.894
I just lost my best friend.

35:06.854 --> 35:08.898
- [sighs]
- His name was Shitara.

35:10.149 --> 35:11.234
He was my bandmate.

35:12.318 --> 35:14.612
We used to live in this dirty apartment.

35:16.739 --> 35:18.658
The venues we played at were small.

35:19.826 --> 35:21.702
Certainly not the stuff of legends.

35:22.578 --> 35:24.122
But we had fun.

35:31.337 --> 35:33.089
By choosing to join this game,

35:34.590 --> 35:37.385
you get to know
who the other players truly are.

35:38.886 --> 35:40.429
It bares their souls.

35:42.473 --> 35:43.683
Like music does.

35:46.102 --> 35:47.145
Maybe I…

35:48.729 --> 35:51.941
just wanted to expose
people's true humanity.

35:56.863 --> 35:59.740
Shitara was a good man,
and a good friend to me.

36:11.377 --> 36:12.795
[chiming]

36:18.009 --> 36:19.051
ARISU
INACTIVE

36:20.428 --> 36:21.512
[Kyuma] Arisu.

36:24.765 --> 36:26.184
You must not forget.

36:28.019 --> 36:29.687
This is a game of life or death.

36:31.439 --> 36:33.191
The losers will die.

36:36.402 --> 36:38.529
Show me what you're made of, Arisu.

36:49.790 --> 36:50.791
[PA chimes]

36:51.417 --> 36:53.794
[computer] Thirty minutes remain.

36:53.878 --> 36:58.007
The King of Clubs team
is currently leading by 12,000 points.

36:59.592 --> 37:00.593
[whirring]

37:00.676 --> 37:01.636
USAGI
INACTIVE

37:03.429 --> 37:05.431
[buzzing]

37:07.808 --> 37:12.438
- Only 30 minutes left.
- And they're up by 12,000 points.

37:12.521 --> 37:15.983
- We can't give up yet!
- [Kuina] We've got to find more items.

37:16.067 --> 37:17.443
[Arisu] It's not worth it.

37:18.194 --> 37:19.570
There's only a few left.

37:20.071 --> 37:21.697
[Kuina] We have to do something!

37:22.198 --> 37:24.659
I'm not sitting here waiting to die.

37:24.742 --> 37:26.911
[Usagi] Tatta still has
over 10,000 points.

37:27.536 --> 37:29.956
- We could pair up and battle--
- [Niragi] Fuck that!

37:30.998 --> 37:33.209
Whose fault is it
we're in this position now?

37:33.751 --> 37:37.129
I'm not trusting this bitch to do anything
after he fucked us!

37:38.589 --> 37:40.716
- Ah, it doesn't matter anyway.
- [sighs]

37:41.342 --> 37:45.179
[Niragi] We can't make up 12,000 points
with little 500-point battles.

37:49.308 --> 37:50.643
If I were Kyuma,

37:52.395 --> 37:53.521
what would I…

38:02.697 --> 38:04.991
ARISU
INACTIVE

38:06.075 --> 38:07.618
[Kyuma] You want the truth, yeah?

38:07.702 --> 38:10.371
Face me with everything that you have.

38:10.454 --> 38:11.831
By choosing to play,

38:13.624 --> 38:16.419
you get to know
who the other players truly are.

38:18.004 --> 38:19.922
This is a game of life or death.

38:20.423 --> 38:22.800
Show me what you're made of, Arisu.

38:28.931 --> 38:30.725
We have to attack their base.

38:32.727 --> 38:33.728
[Kuina] What?

38:34.729 --> 38:38.190
Two of us get 20,000 points
from their base.

38:38.899 --> 38:41.485
- We can still win.
- We can't, man, no!

38:42.028 --> 38:44.238
I was there when they attacked us.

38:44.322 --> 38:45.531
It's impossible.

38:45.614 --> 38:48.784
- What makes you think we can pull it off?
- That's just it.

38:49.744 --> 38:51.579
We have to stop being afraid.

38:52.121 --> 38:53.581
Believe in the plan.

38:54.665 --> 38:56.584
What are you talking about?

38:56.667 --> 38:58.794
[Arisu] The difference between us and them

38:59.337 --> 39:01.297
is whether we let our fear stop us.

39:02.089 --> 39:05.301
We break free, and we push the fear out!

39:07.219 --> 39:09.180
[Usagi] It's too risky. I can't do it.

39:10.556 --> 39:12.808
I won't throw our lives away like that.

39:13.642 --> 39:17.021
But if we don't go,
then we're dead, and that's it.

39:17.813 --> 39:19.940
If we want to win, we have to take a risk.

39:21.317 --> 39:22.526
You're my teammates.

39:23.361 --> 39:24.403
And my friends.

39:25.112 --> 39:27.114
I don't want any of us to die.

39:27.198 --> 39:29.825
But I would risk my life

39:30.951 --> 39:32.620
to be able to save yours.

39:34.580 --> 39:35.790
[Niragi] Well, I'm in.

39:41.295 --> 39:43.631
Not because of all this mushy shit.

39:44.256 --> 39:45.174
It's more.

39:45.966 --> 39:49.470
I'm not the kind of guy
to ever let fear get in my way.

39:53.516 --> 39:54.475
[gasps]

39:55.142 --> 39:56.185
I wanna win.

39:59.021 --> 40:01.065
I can't stand aside. I want to win this.

40:02.316 --> 40:03.442
[sighs]

40:04.735 --> 40:06.112
Then it's settled.

40:08.364 --> 40:10.491
I can't let you take all the glory.

40:10.574 --> 40:11.867
[chuckles]

40:13.577 --> 40:14.537
[Tatta] I…

40:15.996 --> 40:16.914
[sighs]

40:18.791 --> 40:19.667
Tatta.

40:20.793 --> 40:22.294
You protect the base.

40:25.339 --> 40:26.340
Okay.

40:35.307 --> 40:36.976
[yawns]

40:41.105 --> 40:44.567
If we guard this piece of metal,
then we're gonna win.

40:46.652 --> 40:47.778
[sighs]

40:50.448 --> 40:51.449
Huh?

40:53.659 --> 40:55.327
Bet you can't catch me again!

40:56.412 --> 40:57.413
[Goken scoffs]

40:58.998 --> 41:01.500
She's got 50 points left, max.

41:02.334 --> 41:04.462
One more hit and you're a goner!

41:05.546 --> 41:06.714
[gasps]

41:07.339 --> 41:08.466
[laughs]

41:08.549 --> 41:10.009
Goken, wait!

41:10.092 --> 41:11.969
Don't let her provoke you like that.

41:13.053 --> 41:15.681
Come on, victory's ours either way!
[chuckles]

41:22.521 --> 41:23.606
Aah!

41:24.690 --> 41:25.941
[sighs]

41:26.692 --> 41:28.110
[tense, urgent music]

41:29.153 --> 41:30.529
[panting]

41:30.613 --> 41:31.614
Yes, I'm alive!

41:34.825 --> 41:36.744
Let's party!

41:52.718 --> 41:54.053
[Uta] There's another one.

42:25.167 --> 42:26.544
You bored yet?

42:27.503 --> 42:31.382
You must be craving some fun.
You're looking for a rush, aren't you?

42:34.468 --> 42:35.970
You know us so well!

42:36.053 --> 42:37.888
Isn't that right, Arisu?

42:42.351 --> 42:43.852
[energy crackling]

42:44.562 --> 42:46.063
[buzzing]

42:47.231 --> 42:48.148
KYUMA
INFINITE

42:48.649 --> 42:49.483
MAKI
INFINITE

42:50.067 --> 42:51.318
UTA
INFINITE

42:52.444 --> 42:53.737
It'll never work.

43:16.385 --> 43:17.428
[gasps]

43:20.764 --> 43:21.682
Huh?

43:42.328 --> 43:43.579
[panting]

43:54.423 --> 43:56.050
[laughs] Whooo!

43:56.759 --> 43:58.469
[breathing heavily]

44:08.687 --> 44:09.813
All set?

44:10.397 --> 44:11.273
[chuckles]

44:11.357 --> 44:12.316
Uh-huh.

44:12.399 --> 44:13.817
[all gasp]

44:27.456 --> 44:28.999
[screams]

44:31.585 --> 44:33.212
[screams]

44:40.969 --> 44:42.012
Yaah!

44:42.596 --> 44:43.555
[laughing]

44:45.224 --> 44:46.392
[yells]

44:47.851 --> 44:49.019
[thump]

45:08.664 --> 45:10.082
ARISU
INACTIVE

45:10.165 --> 45:11.834
- [electricity crackles]
- [both groan]

45:13.669 --> 45:15.087
You were out of commission!

45:22.636 --> 45:23.804
- [chime]
- [both gasp]

45:28.058 --> 45:29.393
[chimes]

45:29.476 --> 45:32.479
[computer] The scores have been updated.

45:33.897 --> 45:35.649
- The King of Clubs team…
- Yes!

45:35.733 --> 45:36.567
Yes! Come on!!

45:36.650 --> 45:37.985
NIRAGI
INACTIVE

45:38.068 --> 45:39.278
Niragi!

45:42.322 --> 45:44.575
- [electricity crackles]
- [both groan]

45:45.284 --> 45:46.326
Kuina!

45:48.078 --> 45:48.996
Go!

45:49.079 --> 45:50.956
[roars]

45:56.879 --> 45:58.046
[yells]

45:58.130 --> 46:00.090
- [Kuina groans]
- [whirring and chiming]

46:00.674 --> 46:03.677
[computer] The scores have been updated.

46:05.846 --> 46:09.850
The King of Clubs team is now leading
by 3,000 points.

46:09.933 --> 46:11.602
[panting]

46:17.441 --> 46:20.194
- [buzzing]
- [Uta laughs]

46:20.277 --> 46:22.988
Congrats on 10,000!
Too bad it's not enough!

46:23.071 --> 46:24.114
[laughs]

46:24.198 --> 46:25.824
[Kyuma] Well done, Arisu.

46:25.908 --> 46:27.701
Your team had a good go.

46:28.368 --> 46:30.037
But your plan has failed you.

46:31.079 --> 46:33.415
You could get
the remaining items, of course,

46:33.916 --> 46:35.501
but it won't be enough.

46:36.293 --> 46:37.294
[sighs]

46:37.795 --> 46:40.589
[Uta] And we're not giving you
a chance to win now.

46:41.131 --> 46:44.551
We're guarding the base with
everything we've got till time runs out.

46:46.011 --> 46:47.596
- Better accept it.
- [PA chimes]

46:47.679 --> 46:49.932
[Computer] Twenty minutes remain.

46:50.849 --> 46:55.187
The King of Clubs team
is currently leading by 3,000 points.

46:55.270 --> 46:56.313
[sighs]

46:58.190 --> 46:59.441
[sighs]

47:13.163 --> 47:15.249
[sighs] I'm sorry.

47:17.751 --> 47:19.086
This is my fault.

47:22.756 --> 47:23.882
[Arisu] No.

47:25.384 --> 47:26.969
We gave it all we had.

47:29.513 --> 47:31.765
My plan just wasn't good enough.

47:32.516 --> 47:33.517
I'm sorry.

47:35.102 --> 47:37.646
[Niragi] So… So, what? That's it?

47:38.981 --> 47:40.232
[sighs]

47:41.984 --> 47:44.903
Because of you,
we're all gonna fuckin' die, asshole.

47:54.329 --> 47:55.497
[sighs]

47:56.957 --> 47:58.417
I'll look for items.

47:59.334 --> 48:00.711
There's no point.

48:01.837 --> 48:03.714
Maybe not, but I have to do it.

48:05.799 --> 48:06.717
For me.

48:10.637 --> 48:11.847
I have to fight.

48:13.432 --> 48:14.892
See it through to the end.

48:26.486 --> 48:27.821
She's strong.

48:30.198 --> 48:31.658
I sure couldn't do that.

48:46.381 --> 48:47.799
[sobs]

49:07.152 --> 49:09.780
"You're my teammates. You're my friends."

49:10.906 --> 49:12.282
[scoffs]

49:14.326 --> 49:16.161
What a crock of bullshit.

49:18.830 --> 49:19.998
Fuck!

49:21.625 --> 49:23.251
[coughing]

49:27.798 --> 49:28.799
[laughs]

49:30.842 --> 49:32.552
I was so stupid.

49:34.930 --> 49:36.723
[breathing heavily]

49:44.314 --> 49:45.899
Well, either way,

49:46.733 --> 49:48.402
I don't have much time left.

50:40.579 --> 50:42.581
[Arisu gasps]

50:43.165 --> 50:44.958
Isn't there anything we can do?

50:59.806 --> 51:00.807
[gasps] I got it!

51:10.192 --> 51:11.651
- [gasps]
- [PA chimes]

51:11.735 --> 51:14.821
[computer]
The player team has secured an item.

51:17.324 --> 51:21.286
The King of Clubs team is now leading
by 500 points.

51:22.287 --> 51:23.914
Usagi found the final item!

51:26.666 --> 51:28.210
Just 500 to go.

51:29.002 --> 51:30.253
Think! Come on!

51:31.129 --> 51:32.631
We gotta do something!

51:35.801 --> 51:37.761
Kyuma's base… I have to go.

51:37.844 --> 51:39.096
- Why?
- [gasps]

51:39.179 --> 51:41.765
Five hundred.
That's nothing! We can do this!

51:43.225 --> 51:44.142
It's all over.

51:44.226 --> 51:47.562
If I'm going to die,
I'll do everything I can.

51:48.355 --> 51:49.397
[Tatta] Arisu.

51:52.442 --> 51:53.360
Huh.

51:54.069 --> 51:55.153
I have to say,

51:55.737 --> 51:57.697
before I go to at least try…

52:00.617 --> 52:01.618
Tatta.

52:03.370 --> 52:05.122
I love your positive attitude.

52:05.997 --> 52:07.958
You've always cheered me up, Tatta.

52:12.462 --> 52:13.672
Thank you, friend.

52:25.475 --> 52:26.601
[PA chimes]

52:26.685 --> 52:28.353
[computer] Ten minutes remain.

52:28.436 --> 52:32.232
The King of Clubs team
is currently leading by 500 points.

52:32.315 --> 52:33.733
There's still a chance.

52:36.778 --> 52:38.905
[coughing]

52:42.200 --> 52:43.201
Niragi?

52:46.163 --> 52:47.247
[coughs]

52:54.337 --> 52:56.047
Yeah, poor Niragi.

52:57.257 --> 53:01.511
- I found the last item. We just need 500--
- It's a waste of time.

53:02.762 --> 53:04.264
Well, I'm not giving up.

53:08.685 --> 53:09.728
[gasps]

53:10.937 --> 53:12.689
[Niragi] We're all gonna die.

53:13.481 --> 53:14.983
Me, you.

53:17.611 --> 53:20.155
Everyone's gonna die.

53:25.577 --> 53:27.329
You're better than all of us.

53:27.871 --> 53:30.832
That's what you think, isn't it,
that you're better than us, huh?

53:32.667 --> 53:34.169
[grunts]

53:35.629 --> 53:37.589
Am I really so unclean?

53:38.465 --> 53:39.424
Huh?

53:41.301 --> 53:43.511
Everyone looks at me like that now.

53:53.188 --> 53:55.857
[Niragi] I don't know if they hated me
because I was twisted,

53:56.566 --> 53:59.236
or if I became twisted
because they hated me.

54:06.159 --> 54:07.702
I guess Kyuma was right.

54:09.955 --> 54:12.874
Only by facing death
can you learn who you are.

54:14.960 --> 54:16.836
- [breathing unsteadily]
- [Niragi] I get it now.

54:17.754 --> 54:19.089
I know who I am.

54:20.924 --> 54:23.885
I'm not the kind of person
with friends to rely on.

54:23.969 --> 54:25.428
[whimpers]

54:25.512 --> 54:28.390
[Niragi] I'm not the kind of person
with hopes and dreams.

54:30.809 --> 54:31.851
I'm garbage.

54:33.395 --> 54:34.771
- [Usagi gasping]
- [Niragi grunts]

54:36.731 --> 54:38.066
[Usagi yells]

54:42.487 --> 54:43.571
[screams]

54:51.913 --> 54:53.248
[Niragi chuckles]

54:56.668 --> 54:59.170
Me and you can finally finish
what we started!

55:00.088 --> 55:01.464
[strangled gasps]

55:01.548 --> 55:04.259
We can have one last screw,
right here, you and me,

55:04.342 --> 55:06.428
before we go out with a bang! [laughs]

55:06.511 --> 55:07.929
[Usagi whimpers]

55:08.013 --> 55:09.306
- [coughs]
- [gasps]

55:14.102 --> 55:16.104
- [Usagi coughing]
- Usagi!

55:17.063 --> 55:18.690
[screams]

55:20.233 --> 55:21.067
Arisu!

55:21.651 --> 55:23.069
- [whimpers]
- Shut the fuck up!

55:23.153 --> 55:24.070
[gasps]

55:31.619 --> 55:33.455
[breathing heavily]

55:36.916 --> 55:39.461
- [PA chimes]
- [computer] Nine minutes remain.

55:40.128 --> 55:43.590
The King of Clubs team
is currently leading by 500 points.

55:49.637 --> 55:51.639
[urgent, tense music]

56:00.106 --> 56:02.484
[Kyuma] Whooo!

56:06.529 --> 56:08.281
[breathing heavily]

56:19.376 --> 56:21.169
[theme music]
